notesci for Debian / Ubuntu
===========================

notesci ships as a native desktop application (Tauri-built native
binary embedding the React frontend in a WebKitGTK window). When you
launch the app, it spawns the Python backend (uvicorn) as a child
process; closing the app's window kills the backend.

Installation lays out:

  /opt/notesci/bin/notesci    Tauri desktop binary (the launcher)
  /opt/notesci/backend/       Python source (read-only at runtime)
  /opt/notesci/frontend/      Pre-built SPA assets (embedded in the
                              Tauri binary; this dir is also kept as
                              a debugging reference)
  /opt/notesci/venv/          Bundled Python virtualenv (built on
                              install from /opt/notesci/wheels/)
  /opt/notesci/wheels/        Pre-downloaded pip wheels (for offline
                              postinst venv rebuilds)
  /etc/notesci/notesci.conf   Configuration (mode 0640, root:notesci)
  /var/lib/notesci/           Runtime state (currently empty)
  /usr/share/applications/notesci.desktop   App menu entry
  /usr/share/icons/hicolor/.../notesci.png  App icons

Launching
---------

Open the "notesci" entry in your apps menu, or run from a terminal:

  notesci                           # if /opt/notesci/bin is on $PATH
  /opt/notesci/bin/notesci          # absolute

To see backend logs while debugging, launch from a terminal — the
backend's stderr writes to the same terminal.

Configuration
-------------

Edit /etc/notesci/notesci.conf to add LLM provider API keys, then
restart the app:

  sudo nano /etc/notesci/notesci.conf
  # quit and relaunch notesci

The DB password and admin token are auto-generated on first install;
don't change them by hand unless you know what you're doing.

Bootstrap a workspace
---------------------

The first member is created via the operator-only admin endpoint.
With notesci running:

  TOKEN=$(grep NOTESCI_ADMIN_TOKEN /etc/notesci/notesci.conf | cut -d= -f2-)
  PORT=8765   # default — see /opt/notesci/bin/notesci's logs to confirm
  curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:$PORT/admin/workspaces \
    -H "x-admin-token: $TOKEN" \
    -H "content-type: application/json" \
    -d '{"slug":"notesci","name":"notesci","admin_email":"you@example.com"}'

The response contains an invite code; use it in the app's sign-in
screen to create your member account.

Uninstall
---------

  sudo apt remove notesci    # removes /opt/notesci, keeps DB + config
  sudo apt purge  notesci    # also drops the notesci database + role
                              # + removes /etc/notesci + system user

Upgrades
--------

  sudo apt install ./notesci_NEWVERSION_amd64.deb

Config is preserved across upgrades. The venv is rebuilt by postinst
on every install/reinstall (the bundled wheels make this fast and
offline).
